I see the bug. In `dealStock`, I do:
```js
this.columns[col].push({
  card: this.stock.pop(),
  faceUp: true
});
```

But `this.stock.pop()` already returns `{card: {...}, faceUp: false}`, so it creates nested `{card: {card: {...}, faceUp: false}, faceUp: true}`.

The fix: the stock should store plain card objects, or dealStock should unpack them. Let me fix both the stock storage and dealStock:

